.TH TUSER 1 "September 2026" "termux-user-manager 0.2.0" "Termux User Manager"
.SH NAME
tuser \- virtual user/profile management for Termux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuser
COMMAND [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Termux User Manager creates separate HOME, XDG and language/runtime environments
inside Termux. Virtual users are profiles, not real kernel users: all sessions
continue to use the Android/Linux UID of the Termux application.
.PP
The package does not modify the normal Termux HOME or global login scripts.
Virtual homes are created only by an explicit tuser add command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tuser add NAME
Create a virtual user and, by default, a Python virtual environment.
.TP
.B tuser list
List virtual users.
.TP
.B tuser login NAME
Enter a virtual user's login shell.
.TP
.B tuser modify NAME
Modify account metadata, state, shell, groups or explicit environment variables.
.TP
.B tuser delete NAME
Delete account metadata while preserving the home by default.
.TP
.B tuser passwd NAME
Set an optional profile password. This is not a security boundary.
.TP
.B tuser env NAME
Display the environment that tlogin will construct.
.TP
.B tuser runtime python ACTION NAME
Create, enable, disable or explicitly remove the per-user default Python venv.
.TP
.B tuser proot-setup NAME DISTRO
Create and remember a conventional guest-side account inside an installed proot-distro.
.TP
.B tuser proot NAME DISTRO
Bind the virtual home into an installed proot-distro environment and use a remembered guest account mapping when present.
.TP
.B tuser doctor
Check installation and account consistency.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $PREFIX/etc/termux-user-manager/config.json
Package configuration.
.TP
.I $PREFIX/var/lib/termux-user-manager/users.json
Mutable virtual account database.
.TP
.I $TERMUX__ROOTFS_DIR/users/
Default virtual home root. On a standard com.termux installation this is normally /data/data/com.termux/files/users/.
.SH SECURITY
Virtual UID/GID values are metadata only. Filesystem access, processes and Android
permissions are still governed by the single real UID used by Termux.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR direnv (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR python (1),
.BR proot-distro (1)
